A||N||18||TwisT||FOCOA "Kid Danger" Air-Dam...  Come in and see gang!||||14||
Z||000000||TwisT||02-10-2001||06:11 PM||||Ok...<P>I was asked by Sqoach on a different thread what exactly the FOCOA "kig danger" front air dam looks like.  FOCOA doesn't like to show pictures of their stuff for some reason.      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <P>I have this air dam (originally purchased from Gabriel Cayetano) but haven't installed it yet on my '88 GT project.  So I decided I would improvise for you guys and gals...      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>The GT used here isn't mine but is a forum member's (can't remember who,  someone smack me please).  First pic is stock GT:<P>  <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/nokid.JPG">   <BR> <P>Now here's the Kid:<P><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kiddanger2_2.JPG">   <BR>  <P>Of course this is just a computer-enhanced picture,  but very accurate.  The air-dam itself is attached OVER the GT nose,  rather than under it like a lot of others out there that look like they've been just stapled on.  It extends downwards from the original nose only about 4 inches or so.  When installed and seams made smooth,  you wouldn't tell it wasn't factory unless you're a genuine Fiero nut.  It's one of the best looking air-dams I've seen.<P>Now I just have to have enough patience to wait 'till this summer to have it installed,  along with lot's of other goodies.      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Brett<BR>Yankton,  SD<BR>'88 "ITALFIERO" GT<P><p>[This message has been edited by TwisT (edited 02-10-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000001||FieroJoe||02-10-2001||06:16 PM||||ummmm, you used the wrong link somewhere.  I assume that you are using PIP.  Once you have successfully uploaded the pic that you want to post, go directly to that topic and paste the link that PIP automatically puts onto your clipboard.  The link you have posted is the link for PIP to find the correct profile for the Fiero Forum.||||reg||1
