Z||000003||sqoach||02-10-2001||06:49 PM||||that's sweet! i love that. i've seen other ones that had the "hole" in the middle, making it look like it had the bottom part of an original bumper glued on. i love the way that looks. only problem would be those speed bumps  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>they make anything that looks good for the coupe? (84-86)<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig2.JPG"> ||||reg||10
Z||000004||2xsess||02-10-2001||06:57 PM||||looks good but I wonder what the ground clearance on a 1.5" lowered Fiero would be.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>AOL IM : Only2xsess<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2xsess.gif">      <BR> <A HREF="http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html" TARGET=_blank>Visit My Website</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||TwisT||02-10-2001||07:43 PM||||Sqoach,  I don't know what they have available for the coupes...  I guess I've never really looked because I've only had GT's.<P>2xess,  I'm going to find out exactly that this summer.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  Lowering the Fiero when using this air-dam is highly recommended,  despite the obvious ground-scraping stance.  Without lowering,  the Fiero looks awkward with the addition of the air-dam.  (Not just this one;  most look better with lowered suspension)<P>Obviously there are big trade-offs for this...  one of them being "slower than your gramma' driving her Ciera" when you encounter any form of bump.  I for one don't mind the extra hassle...  it's an expected quirk.  <P>Here's yet another I JUST did.  Different angle...  threw in some other mods for fun:<P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kidside.JPG"> <P><BR>I have a whole hard-drive full of this kind of stuff.  Anyone want to see a particular mod,  let me know.  I may start posting some more of my own too.<P>Brett<BR>'88 "ITALFIERO" GT||||reg||1
